class Solution {
public:
    string addBinary(string a, string b) {
        string result;
        int i = a.size() - 1;
        int j = b.size() - 1;
        int carry = 0;

        while (i >= 0 || j >= 0 || carry) {
            int sum = carry;

            if (i >= 0)
                sum += a[i--] - '0';

            if (j >= 0)
                sum += b[j--] - '0';

            result += (sum % 2) + '0';
            carry = sum / 2;
        }

        reverse(result.begin(), result.end());

        return result;
    }
};

Explanation:

We add both binary strings from right to left, just like normal addition. We store the remainder as the current binary digit and carry the quotient to the next position. Finally, we reverse the result to get the correct order.
